      "status": "INCORRECT",
      "xpAwarded": 0,
      "questionText": "[Variation #15] In a binary search tree containing 2047 perfectly balanced nodes, what is the maximum number of comparisons required to search for any element?",
      "explanation": "A perfectly balanced binary tree with $N = 2^h - 1$ nodes has height $h = \\log_2(N + 1)$. Here $N = 2047$, so $h = 11$.",
      "stepByStepSolution": [
        "Formula for max comparisons in balanced BST = height $h = \\log_2(N + 1)$",
        "$N = 2^{11} - 1 \\implies h = 11$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "att-1791611010401-a0aeq",
      "userId": "user-1788625702947-rafjf",
      "questionId": "q-gen-cs-topic-concurrency-24",
      "subjectId": "cs",
      "topicId": "cs-topic-concurrency",
      "conceptId": "concept-cs-topic-concurrency-gen-24",
      "difficulty": "medium_hard",
      "selectedAnswer": "$O(\\log n)$",
      "correctAnswer": "$O(\\log n)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "solvingTimeSeconds": 2,
      "hintsRevealedCount": 0,
      "startedAt": "2026-10-10T05:43:28.401Z",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-10T05:43:30.401Z",
      "status": "CORRECT",
      "xpAwarded": 5,
      "questionText": "[Variation #24] What is the tightest asymptotic time complexity $O(g(n))$ for the following Python algorithm snippet?\n```python\ndef compute_grid(n):\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(25):\n        j = 1\n        while j < n:\n            total += i * j\n            j *= 2\n    return total\n```",
      "explanation": "The outer loop runs a constant number of times $(25)$ which is $O(1)$. The inner loop doubles $j$ each iteration ($j *= 2$), running $\\approx \\log_2(n)$ times. Thus the total complexity is $O(\\log n)$.",
      "stepByStepSolution": [
        "Analyze outer loop: fixed constant bounds $0 \\dots 24$, running $O(1)$ times.",
        "Analyze inner loop: variable $j$ doubles each step, making iterations logarithmic $O(\\log n)$.",
        "Multiply bounds: $O(1) \\times O(\\log n) = O(\\log n)$."
      ]
    },
